{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Document Chunking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def chunk_text(text, chunk_size=200, overlap=50):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    words = text.split()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    chunks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    start = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while start < len(words):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        end = start + chunk_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunk = \" \".join(words[start:end])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunks.append(chunk)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        start += chunk_size - overlap"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return chunks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Hosted Embedding Call"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In production, embedding is a single API call to a hosted model. The response is a fixed-dimension vector per chunk; the math (cosine similarity, top-k) below does not care which model produced the vector."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import os"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import requests"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "EMBEDDING_URL = os.environ[\"EMBEDDING_URL\"]    # gateway URL, e.g. https://llm.internal/v1/embeddings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "EMBEDDING_MODEL = os.environ[\"EMBEDDING_MODEL\"]  # e.g. text-embedding-3-small"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def embed(texts):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    response = requests.post("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        EMBEDDING_URL,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['GATEWAY_TOKEN']}\"},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        json={\"model\": EMBEDDING_MODEL, \"input\": texts},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        timeout=30,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    response.raise_for_status()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [item[\"embedding\"] for item in response.json()[\"data\"]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Cosine Similarity Search"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cosine_similarity(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dot = sum(x * y for x, y in zip(a, b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    norm_a = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in a))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    norm_b = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if norm_a == 0 or norm_b == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return dot / (norm_a * norm_b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def search(query_embedding, stored_embeddings, top_k=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scores = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, emb in enumerate(stored_embeddings):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sim = cosine_similarity(query_embedding, emb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scores.append((i, sim))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scores.sort(key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return scores[:top_k]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Prompt Construction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is where the \"augmented\" in RAG happens. Take the retrieved chunks, format them into a prompt, and ask the LLM to answer based on the provided context."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def build_rag_prompt(query, retrieved_chunks):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    context = \"\\n\\n---\\n\\n\".join("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        f\"[Source {i+1}]\\n{chunk}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i, chunk in enumerate(retrieved_chunks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return f\"\"\"Answer the question based ONLY on the following context."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "If the context doesn't contain enough information, say \"I don't have enough information to answer that.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Context:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "{context}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Question: {query}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Answer:\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: The Complete RAG Pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class RAGPipeline:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.chunks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.embeddings = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def index(self, documents):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        all_chunks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for doc in documents:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            all_chunks.extend(chunk_text(doc))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.chunks = all_chunks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.embeddings = embed(all_chunks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def query(self, question, top_k=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        query_emb = embed([question])[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        results = search(query_emb, self.embeddings, top_k)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        retrieved = [(self.chunks[i], score) for i, score in results]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        prompt = build_rag_prompt("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            question, [chunk for chunk, _ in retrieved]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return prompt, retrieved"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Generation (simulated)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In production, this is where you call the LLM API. For this lesson, we simulate generation by extracting the most relevant sentence from the retrieved context."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def simple_generate(prompt, retrieved_chunks):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    query_words = set(prompt.lower().split(\"question:\")[-1].split())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best_sentence = \"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best_score = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for chunk in retrieved_chunks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for sentence in chunk.split(\".\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            sentence = sentence.strip()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if not sentence:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            words = set(sentence.lower().split())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            overlap = len(query_words & words)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if overlap > best_score:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                best_score = overlap"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                best_sentence = sentence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return best_sentence if best_sentence else \"I don't have enough information.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Experiment with chunk sizes: try 50, 100, 200, and 500 words on the same document set. For each size, run the same 5 queries and count how many return a relevant chunk in the top-3. Find the sweet spot where retrieval quality peaks.\n\n2. Add metadata to each chunk (source document name, chunk position). Modify the prompt template to include source attribution so the LLM cites its sources.\n\n3. Implement a simple evaluation: given 10 question-answer pairs, run each question through the RAG pipeline, and measure what percentage of retrieved chunks contain the answer. This is retrieval recall at k.\n\n5. Build a conversation-aware RAG pipeline: maintain a history of the last 3 exchanges and include them in the prompt alongside the retrieved chunks. Test with follow-up questions like \"What about enterprise?\" after asking about pricing."
      ]
    }
